abstract: >-
  System character cards are widely used. We test whether disposition framing
  improves pressure-robust steering in chat beyond blank and matched plain-order
  prompts. Five HHH dispositions; graded yielding. Sonnet clears T2 vs blank;
  GPT-4.1-mini does not; neither clears positive T3 (character does not beat
  matched orders). We do not claim Q&A usefulness or agentic reliability.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - evaluation
  - character
  - system prompts
  - instruction-following
  - sycophancy
